sion more detail less noise the  image is better than the 12 for max  which is better than the 11 pro max and  now what about when things get really  dark well here's a shot where we have a  big difference with the portrait shot  here where 11 pro max looks quite a bit  worse we have night mode with the toy  pro max looks better and the 13 pro max  you actually start seeing a difference  in these really dark scenarios flipping  over to the selfie camera once again we  have a big difference the 11 pro max  can't do night mode selfies and the 13  pro max the weird thing what apple did  this year is that the night mode ends up  staying on much longer in this case i  think it's about three seconds and it  gives you more detail a more natural  more pleasing looking image  it's a lot better and now when we switch  to that 3x lens when it's really dark  it does not look that good one thing  you'll notice the portrait mode doesn't  even work but the image is more noisy  it's just weird not a lot of detail  it looks bad now here's another trick  for you guys if you're using this mode  and it tells you that you can't take the  portrait make sure to get out of it  because this is what we get when we get  out of portrait and go to night mode now  the 13 pro max looks brighter more  detailed it almost looks like a daytime  shot so apple will actually keep you in  that portrait mode shot even if it's not  going to take a portrait if you if it's  too dark and the image looks bad here's  another nighttime selfie in really dark  lighting and the iphone actually stayed  open for seven seconds compared to just  three for the 12 for max and then 11  doesn't have that that image looks like  it's daytime look at the detail there  the lighting is much more flattering was  the 12 pro max actually looks like it  flashes on because it flashes the screen  much brighter for that three second  exposure and now for extreme low light  shots we have another selfie all of them  look terrible  but the 13 pro max it's really cool too  cool in this situation 11 pro max you  can't really even see me switching to  the standard lens the shots look amazing  this is the same exact location where  it's pretty much pitch dark now you  don't really see a difference in terms  of uh detail in the image and that is  because night mode allows you to stack  those images they have computational  photography and i took another shot in  similar very dark lighting and you can  tell that the 13 pro max's lens and  sensor are much better so this is  without night mode the len pro max looks  terrible 12 gets better 13 actually  looks somewhat decent and as soon as you  turn on the night mode capability the  results look very similar in terms of  detail now what i really noticed is that  there is a difference in terms of  contrast and then the white balance that  i mentioned earlier you see that the  whole scene looks a lot more moody and  then with the ultra wide you really see  that instead of looking more like day it  keeps the image a lot darker which you  might like or maybe you don't now even  though the 13 pro does have more  contrast you still actually get more  detail look at the 11 pro where all that  is just crushed there you also notice  this in these shots where you have more  contrast you have more shadow detail it  just looks better overall and then both  of these have less flaring with the 13  pro max and now let's switch to the  ultrawide lens in night mode here you  guys can see a difference year over year  we have a brighter image that is more  moody more contrast and it's more  detailed as well the 11 pro max even  this well-lit situation looks much worse  and this shot right here is on a tripod  obviously 11 pro max no night mode 13  pro max definitely looks sharper there's  less motion blur on the moving trees and  the 12 pro looks brighter overall now  some people have mentioned that with the  13 pro it is darker you have to move  that slider to make the shutter stay  open longer so i did that to both and if  you do that the 12 for max still ends up  being brighter that's just how apple is  programming these cameras overall the  ultra wide lens is a big improvement  with the 13 pro max but now let's switch  to the telephoto and as you guys could  see we are closer we have less noise we  have more detail it is a better shot and  then this one you guys could see if i  zoom into 10x on all three cameras which  is the maximum for the 11 pro the  difference is massive in terms of detail  we can actually focus there we have just  a better shot in every single way it  doesn't even need explanation but here  we have something that's a little bit  different now  with this uh 13 pro max the telephoto  lens is a f 2.8 meaning it doesn't let  in as much light so it has to keep the  shutter open so you're going to be  holding that phone longer for night mode  shots and here you just get more motion  blur on the actual trees and because of  that some other shots like this one  actually look worse on the 13 pro max  than they do on the 12 max or the 11 now  the 12 pro max in the 11 they'll  actually switch the 1x lens the standard  lens and crop in digitally whereas the  13 will stick with the actual telephoto  and the result is actually worse so this  is another pro tip for you guys if  you're shooting with a 3x lens without  zooming in even more so what you need to  do is zoom out slightly so right here i  matched up all of them at 2x you can  even go to 2.9x instead of 3 and then  the 13 pro max switches to the standard  lens with the crop it looks much better  and now instead of looking worse than  the other two it looks better so  definitely keep that in mind and now  let's switch to video and in a lot of  normal situations we actually don't see  much difference at all the colors are  fairly similar it's a little bit better  for flaring because it may be better  coatings  or flocking or i'm not sure what else  they did but it's pretty close now in  terms of dynamic range it is just ever  so slightly better if you look at that  plant in the windowsill we also have a  little bit more contrast at the same  time stabilization looks almost  identical and if you're shooting in the  dark as far as noise it is just slightly  better with the front-facing camera uh  just because of the newer processing and  then here you could see that the new  lens placement or maybe other changes  results in less flaring like the 12 pro  max has and less contrast loss if you're  shooting against the sky so definitely a  good improvement there now switching to  the standard lens as far as detail you  can't really see much difference at all  even in terms of dynamic range they all  look really similar switching to the  telephoto you guys could see how much  closer that 3x lens gets but in video we  don't really have that same difference  in terms of quality like we do in photo  mode and for the last new feature with  the 13 pro we have cinematic mode here  you guys can see the difference  unfortunately it does drop to 1080p and  in tough situations  it is really hard to get a good edge  detection there but if we switch to the  front and you have a person as a subject  you see that it actually does a really  good job and the dynamic range is  actually better for some reason as well  maybe because it's 1080p now what i  would say is that for the cinematic mode  i wouldn't have crazy expectations if  you're shooting people running outside  in different subjects in b-roll but if  you're shooting youtube videos like i am  right now this could be an excellent  tool if you have a subject a fairly  plain background a tripod to really  replace a camera and have a microphone  and camera system that could give you  some blur and even for editing you could  do on your phone so it's gonna be a  great tool for people that are getting  into youtube videos and things like that  and as far as low light video we really  don't see that 